				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Mobile SDK & Library Vulnerability Tracker\n\nMobile apps bundle dozens of third-party SDKs and native libraries. Each is a potential attack surface — either through **known CVEs** (e.g., the OpenSSL Heartbleed class, Log4Shell in Java-based Android apps) or **malicious package reports** (typosquats, supply chain compromises catalogued by OSSF).\n\nThis page catalogs the libraries we can track with Gt4Security, shows live vulnerability data for each, and documents known malicious SDKs relevant to mobile.\n\nRelated: {{gtPage:Gt4Security — Demo|db=ay32zeq1d68a2o5v8gd9epf14}} | {{gtPage:Gt4Security — CVE Source Comparison|db=ay32zeq1d68a2o5v8gd9epf14}}"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-12T09:52:14.269294-04:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-12T09:52:14.269294-04:00"
					}
