				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "### Not trackable (yet)\n\n- **Pushwoosh** — Russian-linked push notification SDK found in US government/military apps (2022 Reuters investigation). Not a CVE — it's a privacy/espionage concern. No entry in NVD or OSV.\n- **Alamofire / AFNetworking** (Swift/CocoaPods) — OSV doesn't support CocoaPods or Swift ecosystems. NVD has no CPE for these. Would need scraping Apple security advisories.\n- **Firebase** — Google's SDK. Not in OSV Maven; CVEs are tracked under Google's Android Security Bulletins (reachable via our OSV Android ecosystem queries, not per-package).\n- **Mintegral / X-Mode / Igexin** — Ad/analytics SDKs flagged for data exfil or click fraud. Not tracked as CVEs; these are policy violations, not code vulnerabilities."
			},
			{
